@end table

The first word or character command starts at the item's beginning. To read
backwards from its end@comma{} use @kbd{C-e} followed by @kbd{M-b} or @kbd{C-b}. At either end@comma{}
moving outwards repeats the boundary announcement; reversing direction reads
the first or last element again. @kbd{C-a C-f} therefore reads the first character@comma{}
and @kbd{C-e C-b} reads the last. Word and character review share a position.
Selecting another item or changing its displayed value starts a fresh review.

Character review follows your normal capitalisation presentation. If delayed
phonetics are enabled in @ref{Reading Scope And Punctuation,Typing and interaction,,emacsvox,}@comma{} pausing after a character also
speaks its phonetic description. Further input or speech cancels that pending
