.\bin\emacsvox-install.ps1 -Role Desktop -Check
.\bin\emacsvox-install.ps1 -Role Desktop
.\bin\emacsvox.ps1 -Check
@end example

The PowerShell tests use temporary fixtures and an existing native Emacs.
They check doctor behavior@comma{} explicit selections@comma{} prebuilt/offline preflight@comma{}
incomplete installations@comma{} platform rejection@comma{} checksums@comma{} archive paths@comma{} argument handling@comma{} and atomic
configuration replacement.  @code{test/emacsvox-native-bytecode-tests.el} compares
the native inventory with GNU Make and checks dependency order and byte-code
